@spec status_edit_spec  src=tests/specs/status_edit_spec.lua  loc=165  cases=7
@harness   mk

# Intent
  Chrome-level pin for the status bar's editable cells: a segment carrying `set` draws as a
  control rather than text, and both routes into it — the wheel and the InputText — commit
  through `set` clamped to the declared range. Real chrome over a fake imgui; recipe from
  picker_create_spec, with the item, wheel and cursor calls a cell makes added.

# Helpers
  @fn mkChrome(h)  @ 46-49
  @fn mkBar(harness, value, edit)  @ 52-62
      -- A one-cell bar over a value the test can watch. `edit` selects the number behaviour.

# Cases
  @case 'the wheel over a number cell steps by `step` and stops at the declared bounds'  [harness]  @ 66-78
  @case 'part notches accumulate; the wheel only steps on a whole one'  [harness]  @ 82-91
  @case 'step='x2' doubles and halves rather than adding'  [harness]  @ 95-107
  @case 'a display-only cell claims no hit rect; an editable one does'  [harness]  @ 111-121
  @case 'a cell's declared width is its value box; the label sits to its left'  [harness]  @ 125-133
  @case 'a click opens the edit; Enter commits the typed value, clamped'  [harness]  @ 137-149
  @case 'Esc leaves the value alone and closes the edit'  [harness]  @ 153-163

